# Frequently asked questions

## Do agents run in Pontia Cloud?

No. Agent Clients, tools, credentials, and project files stay on your device. Pontia Cloud coordinates identity and remote authorization; an Edge relays encrypted traffic.

## Is a Workspace an operating-system sandbox?

No. Workspace roots limit what the Pontia browser exposes for activation and file discovery. The Agent Client still has the permissions and sandbox policy of its local process.

## How do I access my device remotely?

Sign in to Pontia Cloud, register your device, and open its Remote Dashboard at [app.pontia.dev](https://app.pontia.dev). Follow [Initialization](/docs/initialization) for the complete setup.

## Can Pontia read my prompts or project data?

Pontia has three runtime components:

- **Pontia Cloud** manages users, authentication, device registration, and access authorization. Dashboard traffic flows between the browser and device through an Edge.
- **pontiad** runs on your device, coordinates Agent Clients, and serves prompts and agent data to your Dashboard.
- **Pontia Edge** relays traffic that stays encrypted end to end between the browser and `pontiad`.

Your prompts and project data remain on your device.

## What should I back up?

Back up project files, `$PONTIA_HOME`, and your Agent Clients' native conversation data. Use a trusted encrypted destination for `$PONTIA_HOME`, which contains credentials as well as control state and Workflow files. Follow each Client's backup instructions for its conversation data.

## Does Pontia support Windows?

No. The local control plane supports Linux and macOS 11 or later. Self-hosted Edge supports Linux only.
